1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
This document specifies the requirements for the Employee Data Cleaning project. The project is a Google Colab notebook that loads a messy employee dataset, explores it, finds data quality problems and cleans them using only the pandas library. It is written for the course instructor, the examiner and the author.
1.2 Scope
The project takes one raw CSV file, employee_data_messy.csv, and produces one cleaned CSV file, employee_data_clean.csv. It covers data loading, exploration, missing value handling, text standardisation, type conversion, outlier handling and duplicate removal. It does not cover statistical analysis, visualisation or machine learning.
1.3 Definitions and Abbreviations
•	SRS: Software Requirements Specification.
•	DataFrame: The pandas table structure that holds the data in memory.
•	NaN: The marker pandas uses for a missing value.
•	Median: The middle value of a sorted column. It is not affected by outliers.
•	Outlier: A value that is far outside the normal range, such as an age of 250.
•	Colab: Google Colaboratory, a cloud notebook environment.
